rity and source-author attribution. Repeated submission identity does not certify commands or external effects. The watcher saves start intent/results, exposes uncertain arbitrary execution and states weaker disposable recovery.\n- Lines107–135 preserve authoritative review/check generations, publication, requested work results and requester acceptance. Claims and progress cannot silently satisfy those obligations, and retained prepared meaning survives vocabulary changes.\n- Lines137–205 define activation generations and switch/removal boundaries, reproducible UTC slots, pinned pack/resolved-task meaning, retained bounded missed windows and one accurate missed summary/task. Recoverable firing/effect/frontier coordination prevents duplicate requests and forgotten effects while preserving the shared lease/publication alarm.\n- Lines207–232 otherwise define concrete recipient retention, shared scoped-work units, changed membership, blocked addressees and truthful partial coalescing. Cancellation/supersession is terminal without asserting success. The remaining correction extends this clarity to the non-scoped action case.\n- Lines234–291 make rolling absolute60-minute attempt/retry/member/lane accounting and durable reservations explicit, retain pending hints on exhaustion and coalesce alerts. Independent watcher/C3 work keeps its bounded responsibilities. Endpoints, secrets, route generations and operational records remain private under current authority; rotation/revocation retires old retries. Materialized pack tasks/arguments are scanned and author provenance continues.\n- Lines293–315 correct present-tense watcher availability and retain external-cron, local, hosted and Pi routes, recorded notes, reviewed/landed reports, addressed work and separate publication.\n\nI support the proposed activation/UTC-slot and delivery-count semantics, and the classified informational/scoped coalescing choices, subject to the one non-scoped action clarification. The named owners 